==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|tarif}}, from {{etyl|it|en}} {{m|it|tariffa}}, from {{etyl|ota|en}} {{m|ota|تعرفه|tr=ta'rife}}, from {{etyl|ar|en}} {{m|ar|تَعْرِفَة||tariff, rate}}, from the root {{ar-root|ع|ر|ف}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# a [[system]] of [[government]]-[[impose]]d [[duties]] [[levied]] on [[import]]ed or [[export]]ed [[goods]]; a [[list]] of such duties, or the duties themselves
# a [[schedule]] of [[rate]]s, [[fee]]s or [[price]]s
# {{label|en|British}} a [[sentence]] determined according to a [[scale]] of [[standard]] [[penalties]] for certain [[categories]] of [[crime]]

